# Lenovo IdeaPad fast charge (charge_types) — make it writable without root.
#
# The ACPI battery driver exposes the EC's charge-current policy as
# `charge_types`, a sysfs "list with the active entry in brackets":
#
#   Fast [Standard] Long_Life
#
# Measured on an IdeaPad Slim 5 14IMH10 (61.2 Wh pack), by integrating
# energy_now over 4-minute windows rather than trusting power_now:
#
#   Standard    41.52 W   (~0.7C)   44% -> 49% in 4 min
#   Fast        69.90 W   (~1.0C)   49% -> 57% in 4 min
#
# So this is not a cosmetic knob — it is a 68% swing in charge rate, and
# the reason the panel gets a toggle for it at all.
#
# Owned root:root 0644, so writing it needs root and the drawer's "Fast
# charge" tile would otherwise be a read-only indicator. Same fix, same
# reasoning as 99-ideapad-conservation.rules next door: hand write access
# to `wheel` once at device-add time, so nothing escalates at runtime --
# no pkexec, no password per toggle, no setuid helper. See that file for
# why this is RUN+= and a shell rather than udev's own GROUP=/MODE=
# (those apply to a device NODE in /dev; this is a sysfs attribute).
#
# The one real difference from that rule: NO "bind" action is needed
# here, and DRIVER== would never match. A power_supply device has no
# driver of its own (`udevadm info -a` reports DRIVER==""); it is a class
# device registered by the ACPI battery driver, and charge_types already
# exists on the "add" event. Matching ATTR{type}=="Battery" rather than
# KERNEL=="BAT0" because that name is an ACPI artefact — BAT1 and CMB0
# are both common, and a machine with two packs would need both covered.
#
# The [ -e ] guard is what keeps this a no-op everywhere else: most
# batteries expose no charge_types at all, and the ones that do may not
# offer "Fast". Nothing here asserts the attribute exists.
#
# Installed by scripts/install-hardware.sh (the `./install hardware`
# phase), which also applies the same chgrp/chmod immediately so the
# toggle works without waiting for a reboot.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="power_supply", ATTR{type}=="Battery", \
  RUN+="/bin/sh -c '[ -e /sys%p/charge_types ] && chgrp wheel /sys%p/charge_types && chmod 0664 /sys%p/charge_types'"
